				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "45c418df-aa31-53cb-9a0a-f967b9227231")
	)
	(text "+3V3 / 2 A: FPGA VCCAUX, VCCO 0 and 3, FX3 VIO4 / VIO5 / CVDDQ, front end, 1.8 V LDO"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 337.0055 25.2 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2 2)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "6e7ee7cf-35ef-5053-b753-b9930bd7233b")
	)
	(text "1  Power: USB-C VBUS and the Pi's 5 V through ideal diodes, standby enable, 3.3 / 1.8 / 1.2 V rails"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 15 14 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 3 3)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "78598bd9-4f50-5347-9cf9-0d46cc0ac290")
	)
	(text "The rails run while the Pi's 3.3 V is on OR VBUS is present: diode OR into the buck enables.  In the Pi's STANDBY state\n(5 V on, 3.3 V off) with no USB host, the board is off.  EN = (VBUS - 0.3 V) / 2 from USB (2.0 ... 2.6 V), PI_3V3 - 0.3 V\nfrom the Pi; TPS62A02 EN: high > 1.2 V, abs. max 6.5 V.  The Pi's 3.3 V feeds only this diode, the ID EEPROM and its pull-ups."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 172.9865 33.2 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "7af7d854-9b4b-5995-b4c3-37a333b97bc9")
	)
	(text "Each at its load: +1V2 at the FX3's VDD balls (start-up droop, sheet 3), +3V3A at the comparators, PI_5V / PI_3V3 at the header."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 15 166.763 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "7d8397b1-dfd9-5d0f-a7b7-05a90e963080")
	)
	(text "+1V8 / 0.6 A: the FPGA-FX3 interface (FPGA VCCO 1 and 2, FX3 VIO1-3)"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 208.4189 86.9555 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2 2)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "8315aa7e-ca6e-54d9-9720-c3f0e07c12ce")
	)
	(text "+1V2 / 2 A: FPGA VCCINT, FX3 VDD / AVDD / U3TXVDDQ / U3RXVDDQ"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 15 86.9555 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2 2)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "a166f341-c4fd-5b11-88ca-674dce9c3b71")
	)
	(text "Everything between the FPGA and the FX3 (GPIF II, configuration) runs at 1.8 V: lower switching power and less noise on\nthe FX3's USB 3 PHY (AN70707 section 4.2).  Load about 50 mA: 75 mW in the LDO."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 208.4189 92.7555 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "be76ba94-d40a-55cf-bf12-45c109ae465f")
	)
	(text "Supply test points (top side), with ground pads beside them for a probe's ground spring"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 15 163.163 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2 2)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "c730fce7-a216-50b9-b214-f1bcacddaa1e")
	)
	(text "TPS62A02P and 1 uH, the 1.2 V buck's parts (the TLV62569P and 2.2 uH until 2026-10-26: two part types fewer); 1 uH with\n2 x 22 uF is one of its datasheet's tested filters for VOUT >= 1.8 V (SLUSEG9E table 8-3; 22 uF alone is the standard).\nVOUT = 0.6 V x (1 + 10k / 2.2k) = 3.33 V (values already on the board, so no extra part type; 0.27 mA in the divider).\nLoad about 0.25 A (power estimate); 0.47 A peak to peak in the inductor at 5 V in."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 337.0055 35.4 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "ca86f75e-e287-55f1-b88e-389e80787689")
	)
	(text "TPS62A02P (pin-compatible with the TLV62569P): its reference is +/-1 % for TJ 0 ... 125 C, which the USB 3 rails need (simulated);\n1 uH with 2 x 22 uF, one of its datasheet's tested filters for 1.2 ... 1.8 V (SLUSEG9E table 8-3).\nVOUT = 0.6 V x (1 + 100k / 100k) = 1.20 V: 1.188 ... 1.212 V with VFB +/-1 % and 0.1 % resistors.  FX3: 1.15 ... 1.25 V (and\n1.25 V absolute maximum); XC6SLX9-2 VCCINT: 1.14 ... 1.26 V.  Split sensing: the divider takes the DC level from the FX3's VDD\n(B1V2_SNS, R_SNS beside the FX3), C_FF / C_FB the fast loop from the buck's own output (equal, so that the ratio stays 1:2;\ncrossover 1 / (2 pi x 50k x 440p) = 7 kHz): the 40 mohm of plane to the FX3 drops no DC.  Sensing at the FX3 alone rings at\n160 kHz with the plane's inductance (sim).  R_SNS_L holds the output at 1.2 V if the sense line is open.  The FX3's USB 3 PHY\ndraws up to 0.8 A for 10 us when it starts: it is supplied from its own 100 uF capacitors (sheet 3)."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 15 105.9555 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "cff937ca-a55b-5cba-a550-3de345b9ace1")
	)
	(text "USB-C VBUS and the Pi's 5 V (header pins 2, 4) each reach +5V through an LM66100 ideal diode: either source, or both,\npower the board; neither can feed the other, and the board never powers the Pi.  Each diode's ~CE is on the other source\n(LM66100 datasheet 9.2.1, figure 15): the higher source conducts, make-before-break, and no current flows between them\n(~CE grounded would leave both always on, with no reverse blocking: 8.3.1).  ST, an open-drain status output, unused\nand open (the pin table suggests ground; KiCad's ERC forbids an open collector on the ground flag, and open is harmless).\n1 uF at each diode's input pin (LM66100 datasheet section 11.1).  Capacitance on\nVBUS before soft-started loads: 2 x 1 uF + 2 x 4.7 uF + 100 nF, about 8 uF at 5 V after DC bias (USB: <= 10 uF)."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 15 42 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "ecaab7a6-6e7b-5d12-b6c8-d7fd61028d0c")
	)
